  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/ui/src/headless_gpu.rs` now holds the process GPU lock (`gpu_guard`, `gpu_holders`).\n- A new `headless_gpu::test_gpu(suite)` takes the lock and returns the one device of the process.\n- The device is made one time (`OnceLock`, through `device_for_test` and its SKIP policy). It is never dropped.\n- `tests/trace_composite.rs` and `tests/trace_parity.rs` use `test_gpu` in each test. They do not make their own device now.\n- The lib test `view_pass::tests::fit_target_never_asks_the_device_for_a_texture_past_its_limit` uses `test_gpu`. Before, it made a device with no lock.\n- The three ignored GPU tests take `gpu_guard()` as their first statement:\n  - `render_all_guide_images` (`tests/guide_images.rs`)\n  - `review_1710_wcs_page_and_viewport_evidence` (`tests/review_1710_evidence.rs`)\n  - `generate_evidence_screenshots` (`viewport_bar_tooltip_tests.rs`)\n- `egui_app::gpu_test_lock` re-exports the lock from `headless_gpu`. The lib tests and the shared device take the same one lock.\n- `docs/decisions/3605-gpu-test-device-lock.md` records the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nEach test in the two trace binaries made and dropped its own wgpu device. The tests run on parallel test threads with no lock. On a hybrid-GPU Windows laptop (Intel Arc 140T + NVIDIA RTX 5050), two or more devices were alive at the same time. Both binaries ended with `0xC0000005`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (lib, `egui_app::gpu_test_lock`):\n- `devices_asked_from_many_threads_are_one_device_used_one_at_a_time`: 8 threads ask for the device 4 times each, at the same time. Each must be the only holder. All must get the same device. Each makes a buffer and submits under the lock.\n- `the_trace_binaries_share_one_locked_device`: a source scan. `trace_composite.rs` and `trace_parity.rs` must call `test_gpu` and must not call `device_for_test(`, `headless_gpu::device(` or `request_device(`.\n- `every_gpu_test_takes_the_lock`: the table now has 12 tests (4 new). Each must start with `gpu_guard()` or take `test_gpu`.\n\nRed before the fix, and mutation results (each restored after, then green):\n- Old call sites (the six test files from `upstream/main`): `the_trace_binaries_share_one_locked_device` FAILED (`tests/trace_composite.rs: takes the shared device through test_gpu`). `every_gpu_test_takes_the_lock` FAILED (`view_pass.rs: ... found \"let Some(gpu) = crate::headless_gpu::device_for_test(...)\"`).\n- Lock removed (`gpu_guard` locks a new mutex each call): `devices_asked_from_many_threads_...` FAILED alone (`a second test holds the GPU`). `the_lock_lets_one_holder_in_at_a_time` and `a_panic_with_the_lock_held_...` FAILED too.\n- Shared device removed (a new device for each call): `devices_asked_from_many_threads_...` FAILED (`one device for the process, found 6`).\n\nCommands on the final head `204e7c003`:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 13 steps, 0 failed (ui lib, trace_composite, trace_parity, catalog_render and the other ui suites).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: the diff reaches no heavy lane (0 steps).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The diff changes only test support and tests in `camcraft-ui`. No post, toolpath or catalog code changed, so the `example_catalog` suites are not reached. No snapshot PNG changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **Windows verification pending on a hybrid-GPU box.** I ran on macOS (Metal) only. The merging session runs the two trace binaries and the ui lib tests on the Intel Arc + NVIDIA laptop.\n- The three ignored evidence renderers were not run. They need opt-in env vars and write PNGs. Only their first statement changed.\n\n## #3379\n\nRefs #3379. This PR likely covers part of #3379. The ui lib binary had one more test that made a GPU device with no lock (`view_pass::tests::fit_target_never_...`, added for #3582). That test now takes the shared, locked device. I cannot prove that this was the cause of the 12-thread `STATUS_ACCESS_VIOLATION` without the Windows box. I did not claim #3379.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone. No open PR changes these files.\n\nChangelog: none (test support only; no user-visible change)\n\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #3605\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
